# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-16, R-6, RC-5; L §5.19 Readings at a place that keeps parts). L §5.19: "a negative gap is a take of its size by an outflow nobody knows, so the
# order's terms on w are holes, its terms on k still rank, and the take is undecided as far as the terms on w reach". The
# anchor states 120.00 over 150.00 booked (gap -30.00); first in first out ranks by k alone, so the take is b1's 30.00
# (b1 70.00, b2 50.00; scratch/exp7.py).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind lots: place PLN min 0
  batched
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order k.batch.day
place konto: lots lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input b1_day: date
input b1_amt: money PLN
input b2_day: date
input b2_amt: money PLN
move b1: transfers
  on b1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount b1_amt
move b2: transfers
  on b2_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount b2_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of b1, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of b2

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  b1_day = 2026-02-01
  b1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  b2_day = 2026-02-15
  b2_amt = 50.00 PLN

version stmt
  cite s
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-04-01
  anchor konto
  stated[konto] = 120.00 PLN at 2026-03-31 end
=== expect
q: (120.00 PLN, 70.00 PLN, 50.00 PLN)
  anchor: konto 2026-03-31 end, stated 120.00 PLN, difference -30.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-01
